{"hw":"οὐδαμός","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">οὐδαμός</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">οὐδαμ-ός</span>, <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ή</span>, <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">όν</span>, for <span class=\"gk\">οὐδὲ ἀμός</span>, <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">not any one, no one</b>, like οὐδείς, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.D.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pron.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">57.2</span> </span>: used only in pl. and only by <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Ion.</span> </span> writers ( <abbr>=</abbr> <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Att.</span> </span> <span class=\"gk\">οὐδένες</span>)<span class=\"gk\">, οὐδαμοί, οὐδαμῶν</span>, etc., <b class=\"lex-tr\">none</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.18</span> </span>,<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24</span> </span>,<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">57</span> </span>, al.; <span class=\"gk\">πρήγματα.. οὐδαμῶν Ἑλληνικῶν τῶν οὐ πολλὸν μέζω</span>, i.e. much greater than any Greek power, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.145</span> </span>: rarely in fem., <span class=\"gk\">οὐδαμὰς ἄλλας</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.114</span> </span>.—Cf. <span class=\"gk\">μηδαμός</span>.</div></div>"}